cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Scm2Cpp: A Scheme-to-readable-C++ translator with type inference"
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Niitsuma
    given-names: Hirotaka
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8746-1595"
    affiliation: "Osaka Metropolitan University College of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/niitsuma/scm2cpp"
abstract: >-
  Scm2Cpp translates a subset of Scheme into C++ that a person can read and
  edit. Unlike conventional Scheme compilers, which treat C as a portable
  assembler, it gives Scheme values no runtime representation: types come from
  whole-program Hindley-Milner inference, and whatever inference cannot resolve
  becomes a C++ template parameter. Because the emitted loops are ordinary for
  loops, they can carry OpenMP or OpenACC directives or be rewritten as Thrust
  algorithms, all selected from the command line.
keywords:
  - Scheme
  - C++
  - source-to-source translation
  - type inference
  - Hindley-Milner
  - Racket
  - parallel computing
license: MIT
